>> title: Baked Ziti
>> category: Pasta
>> tags: pasta, tomato, ricotta, mozzarella, italian, oven, baked
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: ziti, baked pasta, ziti al forno, pasta al forno, baked ziti with ricotta
>> pairs-with: marinara-sauce, meatballs
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.2: boil 3 min under the box
>> step.3: beat the ricotta with an egg
>> step.4: toss the hot pasta through both
>> step.5: layer with mozzarella, half in the middle
>> step.6: bake 375°F (190°C) 35 min, uncovered at the end

Preheat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C) ~preheat{15%min}.

Boil @ziti{1%lb}(450 g) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{2%Tbs} ~boil{7%min}, three minutes short of what the box says, then drain it.

Beat @whole-milk ricotta{15%oz}(425 g) with @egg{1%large}(50 g), @grated parmesan{1/2%cup}(50 g), @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and @fresh basil{2%Tbs}(chopped). The egg is what stops the ricotta going grainy and weeping under the heat.

Toss @&(~2)drained ziti{} through @&(~1)ricotta{} and @marinara sauce{4%cup}(950 mL; from the recipe on this shelf) while the pasta is still hot enough to steam.

Layer @&(~1)dressed ziti{} into a buttered #9x13-in dish{} with @low-moisture mozzarella{12%oz}(340 g; grated), half of it buried in the middle of the pasta and half over the top.

Bake @&(~1)dish{} covered with foil ~bake{20%min}, then uncover it and ~bake{15%min} more, until the top has browned in patches and the edges are bubbling.

Boil it three minutes short. Ziti drinks a good deal of the sauce in the oven and properly boiled it arrives as paste.
